30,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It seems usage is heavily skewed toward those nearest the door, and eating at desks is creating a mess.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are sobering. We have almost no unplanned social interaction, and private conflicts are handled publicly.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"A hot lunch takes twenty-five minutes round trip, and the old fridge was a disaster of abandoned food.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"We spent 68,000 yen on tiny outside rentals last year. A meeting fit-out is 141,000, while a kitchen is 96,000.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The wall is mere plasterboard; everything is heard. Interestingly, the empty store room has had zero facilities issues.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the outside hire cost suggests a strong need for a private meeting space.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"But a meeting space is formal. We need a place for the ""unplanned"" and the ""awkward"" to be resolved.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"If we have a kitchen, we stop the crumb problem at the desks and save time on lunch trips.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"A kitchen is cheaper to install, but does it solve the rental cost for meetings?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,A kitchen might increase the noise and mess that the thin walls already struggle to contain.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A quiet room would solve the noise, but it doesn't address the rental costs or the food issue.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"A quiet room provides the sanctuary we lack, though perhaps not the social bridge I hoped for.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Servas, surely a bit of noise is better than the sterile silence we have now?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,Let's be rational. We are paying for outside rooms because we have no internal meeting space.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,And we are eating at our desks because we have no kitchen. Both are inefficiencies.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We must choose the option that solves the most pressing systemic failure.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe the lack of a private space for communication is the most profound failure.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I still think the daily grind of lunch and cleaning is the most immediate annoyance.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,The financial drain of outside hire is the most objective problem.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,We must balance the need for utility with the need for peace.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The options are an Open Kitchen, a Quiet Room, or a Meeting Space. I lean toward the Meeting Space.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"A Quiet Room would offer peace, but a Meeting Space allows for the private conversations we desperately need.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,I'm voting for the Open Kitchen. It improves daily life and stops the desk crumbs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,The Meeting Space is the only choice that stops the monthly financial leak.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Given the thin walls, a Quiet Room is the only way to ensure actual tranquility.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, the kitchen doesn't solve the problem of where to have a private professional discussion.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, a Quiet Room is for solitude, but we need a place for dialogue.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, is 68,000 yen really more important than our daily comfort and hygiene?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"In a business sense, yes. It's a recurring cost that a one-time fit-out eliminates.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Comfort is not just about food, May; it is about the mental space to work without distraction.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I believe the Meeting Space is the most versatile and logically sound choice.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I will concede to the Meeting Space if it means we can finally have private conversations.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,I can't get behind a meeting room when we're still trekking for lunch.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,The numbers don't lie. The Meeting Space is the rational investment.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I still prefer the Quiet Room, but I see the consensus forming.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Let us vote.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine, let's see where we stand.","{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let's settle this.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,I am ready.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
